(172,"Ch 20 to 39",["He had come north to do something about it, and he also believed nobody could do anything about it. Until now, those two facts had never sat next to each other in his head.", "Instead he stood there with the keys and thought about the logs", "He wanted to draw a line through it and extend it. Instead he opened the inbox.", "he had stopped sleeping for a month. This time he read it standing up, with the coffee going cold.", "He'd come with a better plan, and he had it on his phone.", "every fifteen minutes. It was already priced. He showed her.", "He didn't sleep. All night he lay in the shouse with the phone on his chest", "The stove ticked as it cooled, and he listened to it until the window went gray.", "A fix would be drafted by March. He had, everyone knew, already started.", "Then the red light came on. From somewhere outside himself he watched himself skip to the last slide", "into the microphone. When he sat down, eight minutes of the talk were still unsaid.", "What he wanted was numbers, and he had a notebook of them already.", "He knew what he was doing. There was a name for it in the notebook, and a rule against it. For three nights he did it anyway.", "Nobody got a plan from him. At a Friday table he had said out loud that he was done bringing plans, and Wren had put her hand on her chest.", "There was the date in the corner, the one with his initials", "He didn't tell anyone. There was nothing he could show them.", "So he closed the notebook and snapped a rubber band around it.", "He wanted to argue, to run it again with the fix in, right now, and show everybody it worked. Then he looked at Irene.", "Nate and Wes had given it to him, and his mother, and David across a bar.", "Curtis stood up. Without a word, he wiped his mouth", "That room had told him no before.", "So he sat there with the laptop pointed at her shoulder.", "Eleven notebooks about a machine, and not one line about that. He never thought about it, because", "The second it was out, he heard how it sounded. What he meant was that he wished", "Twice, on the way to the feed store, he drove past the turn and didn't take it.", "It took him a minute to tune it, and it slipped, and he tuned it again.", "Afterward he leaned the guitar back in its corner and put the blanket back on.", "From down there he lifted the hose over his head with one hand", "For this he cashed the newest one.", "That one went without a note.", "He knew what it was, and had known since a hinge and a gatepost in July.", "From now on he would have to be careful in here, more careful than he used to be.", "Eleven notebooks rested on it.", "He meant the part about another time. The phone went back in his pocket.", "He drank half and tipped like a man who used to get tipped. He took the book out"],["He had come north to do something about it. He also believed nobody could do anything about it. He had never put those two facts next to each other.", "He stood there with the keys and thought about the logs", "He stayed where he was useful. Useful was easier than David.", "He swept the shop twice. He checked his phone for nothing. He thought about a field full of people who could dance", "He wanted to draw a line through it and extend it. He opened the inbox.", "he had stopped sleeping for a month. He read it standing up, with the coffee going cold.", "He read it three times. He typed I'm sorry I missed and looked at it", "He pocketed the phone to answer later, when he could think, and went to find Grace.", "He'd come with a better plan. He had it on his phone.", "every fifteen minutes. He'd already priced it. He showed her.", "He didn't sleep. He lay in the shouse with the phone on his chest", "The stove ticked as it cooled. He lay there and listened to it until the window went gray.", "He'd have a fix drafted by March. He had, everyone knew, already started.", "Then the red light came on. He watched himself skip to the last slide", "into the microphone. He sat down with eight minutes of the talk unsaid.", "He wanted numbers. He had a notebook of them already.", "He knew what he was doing. He had a name for it in the notebook and a rule against it. He did it for three nights anyway.", "He didn't bring anybody a plan. He had said out loud, at a Friday table, that he was done bringing plans. Wren had put her hand on her chest. He had asked Grace", "He looked at the date in the corner, the one with his initials", "He didn't tell anyone. He had nothing he could show them.", "He closed the notebook and snapped a rubber band around it.", "He wanted to argue. He wanted to run it again, with the fix in, right now, and show everybody it worked. He looked at Irene.", "He put the hinge down on the post. He was back in a hallway", "He had gotten it from Nate and Wes, and from his mother, and from David across a bar.", "Curtis stood up. He didn't say a word. He wiped his mouth", "He had heard no in that room before.", "He sat there with the laptop pointed at her shoulder.", "He had eleven notebooks about a machine and not one line about that. He never thought about it. He didn't think about it because", "He heard how it sounded the second it was out. He meant that he wished", "He drove past the turn twice on the way to the feed store and didn't take it.", "He tuned it, and it slipped, and he tuned it again.", "He leaned the guitar back in its corner and put the blanket back on.", "He lifted the hose over his head with one hand", "He cashed the newest one for this.", "He didn't put a note in that one.", "He knew what it was. He had known since a hinge and a gatepost in July.", "He would have to be careful in here now, more careful than he used to be.", "He'd built eleven notebooks on it.", "He meant the part about another time. He put the phone back in his pocket.", "He drank half. He tipped like a man who used to get tipped. He took the book out"]),
(173,"Ch 33, 34, 38",["\"Owned by who?\" Curtis said, not looking up from his plate.", "\"Name one,\" Marta said, and set her cup down.", "\"Easy for you,\" Curtis said, sitting back in his chair.", "\"Most of them,\" Denny said, raising his glass.", "\"Nine days,\" Curtis said, looking out the windshield.", "\"Item four,\" Reuben said, turning a page.", "\"Hell, I'll look at it,\" said Lou, and held out his hand for the laptop.", "\"That's a thermometer, Curtis,\" Frank said, rubbing his eyes.", "\"I know,\" Tyler said, looking at his plate.", "\"Sit down, Curtis,\" Rosa said, and patted the bench beside her."],["\"Owned by who?\" Curtis said.", "\"Name one,\" Marta said.", "\"Easy for you,\" Curtis said.", "\"Most of them,\" Denny said.", "\"Nine days,\" Curtis said.", "\"Item four,\" Reuben said.", "\"Hell, I'll look at it,\" said Lou.", "\"That's a thermometer, Curtis,\" Frank said.", "\"I know,\" Tyler said.", "\"Sit down, Curtis,\" Rosa said."]),
(174,"Ch 32, 34, 35, 38",["\"Curtis, it's an arm. It's bolted", "This time nobody said yes. There were three tables now, at one table.", "But it didn't break. Somebody did it on purpose."],["\"It's not the Terminator, Curtis. It's an arm. It's bolted", "\"It's not that they can't. It's that they won't.\"", "This time it wasn't a yes. It was three tables now, at one table.", "But it didn't break. It's on purpose."]),
