(178,"Ch 37",["It took a morning. A bag of clothes went in, and the laptop. Then a milk crate of notebooks, eleven of them now, and the manuscript, which was three hundred pages and had a title. He stood holding that one a while before he set it down. The broken coupons went in a coffee can. His mother's pot went in beside them. Going on three years, and everything he owned fit in the bed of the Ranger with room left over."],["It took a morning. A bag of clothes. The laptop. A milk crate of notebooks, eleven of them now, and the manuscript, which was three hundred pages and had a title. The broken coupons, in a coffee can. His mother's pot. Everything he owned fit in the bed of the Ranger with room left over, except two robot arms in the back of the equipment shed."]),
