(232,'Ch 27, 38',['Rosa made the dinner that year, her first for the farm.', "Curtis asked her where she'd learned to cook for forty.", '"I had a big family, but life, it get away from us. The love is still there, deep down, even if the finances maybe get in the way sometimes," Rosa explained.', '"I know someday I cook for my family again. But maybe sometimes is ok to give love a little breathing room."', 'She set a casserole dish on its trivet, and the feast began.', '"But this last year I volunteer at the church kitchen and we cook a lot of food, I cook all day, and now I cook all day here for you!"', 'Lou started the clapping, and the whole trailer took it up.', 'she took a rosary out of her apron pocket, held it in her good hand, and said grace.', 'Bendícenos, Señor, y bendice estos alimentos que por tu bondad vamos a recibir. Por Cristo nuestro Señor. Amén.', 'He had built the holiday route into an app the night before', 'In one ear, out the other.', 'I do know good food.', 'You have the heart of a helper. I can tell.', '"I just want everybody to be prepared," Elijah said.', 'Prepared is sometimes not helpful.', 'If I over-prepare my tamales, they fall apart.', 'Elijah kind of got it.', 'It\'s her turn to eat."\nAfter the kitchen trailer fed forty,', 'And Rosa, in a good blouse, with her wrist out of the brace'],['And Rosa, at her first dinner,']),
